# The image is built from source, not from the machine that built it.
#
# `node_modules` is the load-bearing entry: the Dockerfile installs into the
# build stage, and copying the host's tree over it layers darwin binaries into
# a linux image and shadows that install.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# `local/` is the candidate's own data — stories, transcripts, drill-log. It is
# a mounted volume in a deployed instance and must never be baked into an image
# other people pull.
local

.git
.gitignore
.claude
voice/dist
voice/dist-demo
